{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nEighteen provider, lifecycle, build, cache, and tracing test modules contain 48 audited prose blocks: 39 leading docstrings and 9 full-line comment regions (4,880 before-words), frozen at `origin/main@d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84`. Revalidation keeps the current `structured_run._import_pydantic_ai` seam and the current `bridge status` literal; neither executable correction is prose scope.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only the frozen prose blocks below. A `D:<owner>` is the leading `Expr(Constant(str))` in a `Module`, `ClassDef`, `FunctionDef`, or `AsyncFunctionDef`. A `C:<scope>:before:<anchor>` is one maximal consecutive full-line COMMENT-token region, owned by the innermost AST scope and anchored to the next unchanged non-comment code. Compact `D{a,b}` and `C{scope@anchor,...}` notation expands to those exact IDs under the row's path; the reviewer writes the fully path-qualified `<path>#<ID>`.\n\nFor every owned path, retain immutable before and final blobs and parse both with `ast.parse(..., type_comments=True)`. On comparison copies remove only allowlisted leading docstring nodes; normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; require the remaining `ast.dump(..., include_attributes=False)` values to match. Tokenize both blobs and reject changed inline comments or non-allowlisted full-line comments. Preserve runtime strings, regexes, prompts, imports, decorators, annotations, assertions, subprocess arguments, test data, shebangs, and complete directive-bearing physical lines exactly. Only adjacent blank-line normalization around an edited block is allowed.\n\n## Stable block allowlist\n- `tests/unit/test_bedrock_provider.py` — `D{<module>,test_supports_temperature_defaults_true_for_everything_else,test_warns_when_caching_was_requested_but_both_counters_are_zero,test_bedrock_builder_sets_exactly_the_two_parity_cache_keys,test_bedrock_model_id_config_field_is_gone,test_bedrock_region_knob_is_untouched,test_default_model_opus_4_8_withdraws_temperature,test_sonnet_retains_temperature_support,test_direct_anthropic_opus_also_withdraws_temperature,test_botocore_still_ignores_aws_region_but_rebar_now_closes_the_trap,test_this_checkout_pins_the_region_beside_its_region_scoped_model_pins}`; `C{<module>@def _stub_bedrock_provider,<module>@@contextlib.contextmanager,<module>@def _spy_boto_session,<module>@def _region_pinned_project}`\n- `tests/unit/test_blocking_relation_partition.py` — `D{<module>,test_neither_site_re_lists_relation_names}`\n- `tests/unit/test_blocking_severity_retirement_docs.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_bridge_projects_surfaces_heldout.py` — `D{<module>,test_bridge_projects_set_commits_and_leaves_a_clean_tree}`\n- `tests/unit/test_bug_blast_radius_escalation_ad0d.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_bug_claim_rca_sequence_docs.py` — `D{<module>,test_claim_time_exemption_type_registry_includes_bug}`\n- `tests/unit/test_bug_review_tier.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_bugfix_repeat_fix_1dd5.py` — `D{<module>,test_the_gate_honours_an_explicit_window_anchor}`; `C{<module>@_DIFF}`\n- `tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py` — `D{<module>,test_unescalated_under_threshold_diff_never_reads_the_store,test_classify_unpinned_signing_environment_is_accepted}`; `C{<module>@_GATE_OWN}`\n- `tests/unit/test_build_drift.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_build_provenance.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_c3b_push_defer_coupling_heldout.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_cache_floor_per_model.py` — `D{<module>,test_large_total_with_tiny_marked_prefix_warns_and_names_the_marked_prefix}`\n- `tests/unit/test_cache_floor_warning.py` — `D{<module>,test_no_warning_below_the_cacheable_prefix_floor,test_still_warns_at_or_above_the_floor_when_both_counters_are_zero,test_the_floor_has_a_single_shared_definition}`; `C{<module>@@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"input_tokens\",...)}`\n- `tests/unit/test_cache_prefix_breakpoint.py` — `D:<module>`; `C{test_effective_cache_prefix_is_the_single_validity_predicate@assert _req(_PREFIX).effective_cache_prefix() == _PREFIX}`\n- `tests/unit/test_canary_bridge_wiring.py` — `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_candidate_tracing_oracle.py` — `D{<module>,_install_native_downgrade}`; `C{<module>@<EOF>}`\n- `tests/unit/test_candidate_tracing.py` — `D:<module>`\n\n## Protected false positives\nAll unlisted prose is protected, especially the concise full-length/proper-prefix comment before the second assertion in `test_effective_cache_prefix_is_the_single_validity_predicate`. Preserve every noqa/type-ignore/pragma directive, provider/model/config literal, measured counter/value, external URL, and assertion. The published cache-floor URL and model/floor table inside the allowlisted module docstring remain exact facts.\n\n## Preserved contracts and consumers\nKeep measured Bedrock cache/temperature/region/retry behavior; canonical relation partition and retired severity posture; bridge-project parity and committed-clean writes; blast-radius/repeat/size bug escalation plus claim-RCA sequence; ancestry/provenance rules; live push-mode reads; per-model marked-prefix cache floors; canary delegation; and candidate span failure/sanitization/nesting contracts. Real source/path consumers include `test_attestation_signing.py`, `test_web_tool_gating.py`, and `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_operation_snapshot_authoritative_binding.py`; the candidate oracle imports its owned harness. External provider/tracing modules remain documented consumers but are not added to the non-external focused command. No target docstring consumer was found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Only the declared stable-ID blocks and adjacent blank lines change; the AST and token/comment comparisons pass on every owned path.\n- [ ] Every edited block is shorter and retains the listed current contract while removing chronology, duplication, obvious narration, or separator ornament.\n- [ ] A non-author reviewer posts exactly 48 leaf-linked TSV rows: `stable_block_id<TAB>before_citation<TAB>final_citation<TAB>preserved_contract_or_consumer<TAB>directives_exact<TAB>before_words<TAB>after_words<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer_session`.\n- [ ] Before citations use `d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84:<path>#<stable-id>`; final citations use `<final-commit-sha>:<path>#<stable-id>`; every row has `after_words < before_words` and records `directives_exact=PASS`, `semantic-preservation=PASS`, and `bloat-removal=PASS`.\n- [ ] All five structured verify commands pass.\n\n## Verification\nThe five DD-level commands recorded on this ticket run focused pytest with real consumers, scoped Ruff check plus format-check, comment hygiene, owned-path `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv `make verify`. They are the executable completion oracle."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788626486610835151,"uuid":"ed513f1b-5f9b-4e12-955c-61da4dad3748"}